"Eldrin Fume Filters": {
  "index": 0,
  "category": "artifice",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Eldrin Fume Filters"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Eldrin Fume Filters",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " allow me to "
        },
        {
          "text": "burn motes or sachets to generate a small trickle of Eldrin Power",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  Anything that burns in a furnace should be usable as fuel.\n\nThe Eldrin Power will feed directly into my reserves and does not need to be captured by external apparatus. However, "
        },
        {
          "text": "this fume filter does not supply Eldrin Power to things that require it",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I still must use "
        },
        {
          "text": "Conduits",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " for that purpose.\n\nThe mote, once any smoke has gone through it, binds to the fume screen and renders it unusable in any other circumstance.\n\nThe trade-off is that a mote will burn for a very long time before needing to be replaced. Interestingly, breaking the fume or using a different kind of mote will disperse any residual traces of a mote used prior, resulting in its loss."
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nFume filter output can be increased in two main methods: "
        },
        {
          "text": "attaching Fume Bellows to one or both adjacent sides of the fume filter, or capturing wellsprings.",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "  Fume filter output can be altered using a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Fume Prism.",
          "color": "blue"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
